KZ2 patch 6052: FSR 1 before the HUD (the pre-HUD tap of KZ3 patch 2145's interface, rsx_upscale_pre_hud).

Killzone 2's frame draws the HUD into the display buffer in a run of its own: lights and colour grading into the
2560x720 sample buffer, ONE resolve draw into the display buffer, the half-res chain, the next frame's G-buffer, then
the HUD draws into the display buffer again, before the flip (gated draw captures, the RE notes rounds 20 and 67b).
So the display buffer's second visit in a frame (a draw into it after draws into another surface) is where the HUD
starts. There, with UPSCALING = FSR 1 and a window larger than the display buffer:
- FSR 1 (EASU + RCAS) enlarges the display buffer, the finished scene without HUD, into an output-size target
  (R8G8B8A8 RT|UAV, the scaling rectangle's size), and an output-size depth target is cleared;
- every later draw and colour clear of that display buffer in the frame goes to that target, viewport and scissor
  scaled by output/display size: the HUD is drawn at output resolution, not upscaled;
- the present copies the target 1:1 (rsx_upscale_tapped: no second pass); the scan-out gamma runs on it.
The rule is libs/video/rsx_pre_hud.h (pure; host test tools/runtime/test_pre_hud.sh walks Killzone 2's frame).
A frame with no second visit (loading, movies) keeps patch 6051's FSR at present; the front end has two visits and
is tapped too (its later draws are drawn at output size). Logged: the first tap,
every 600 frames the counts of taps / HUD draws / clears, any HUD draw that tests depth or stencil or reads WPOS.
LD_UPSCALE_PRE_HUD=0 restores 6051's behaviour (FSR at present on the composed image). RSX_UPSCALE_AB=<s> (test aid):
the choice cycles every <s> seconds through off / FSR 1 before the HUD / FSR 1 at present, one line per change, for
same-run A/B where the menu is out of reach (in play).
Also: rsx_upscale_d3d12.c with a caller-provided output re-made its intermediate only when none existed, so after a
window resize an at-present evaluation's old-size intermediate was used (a fix for KZ3 2145 too).

